# 🏛 Unified Laravel Enterprise Architecture Guide

System-Level Rule File for AI & Developers

This document is the single source of truth for architecture, coding
standards, UI rules, and AI behavior. All generated code must comply
100%. No exceptions.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1️⃣ Environment & Stack

## Core Stack

-   PHP 8.4.16
-   Laravel 12
-   MySQL (STRICT -- PostgreSQL removed)
-   HTML
-   CSS
-   JavaScript
-   Offline-first development
-   No external runtime dependencies

## Laravel Ecosystem Versions

-   laravel/framework v12
-   pestphp/pest v4
-   phpunit/phpunit v12
-   laravel/pint v1
-   laravel/sail v1
-   laravel/prompts v0
-   laravel/mcp v0

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 2️⃣ Global Architecture Model

The project enforces:

-   Clean Architecture
-   Layered Architecture
-   MVC (Presentation layer only)
-   Domain-Driven Design (DDD)
-   SOLID Principles
-   Strict inward dependency rule

Dependencies MUST flow inward only.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 3️⃣ Layer Structure (STRICT ORDER)

1.  Presentation\
2.  Application\
3.  Domain\
4.  Infrastructure

No reverse dependency allowed.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 4️⃣ Required Project Structure

app/ ├── Domain/ │ ├── Entities/ │ ├── ValueObjects/ │ ├── Aggregates/ │
└── Repositories/ (Interfaces only) │ ├── Application/ │ ├── UseCases/ │
├── DTOs/ │ └── Services/ │ ├── Infrastructure/ │ ├── Persistence/ │ ├──
Repositories/ (Implementations) │ └── Services/ │ ├── Presentation/ │
├── Controllers/ │ ├── Requests/ │ └── Views/

Domain MUST be framework-independent.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 5️⃣ Clean Architecture Rules

✔ Business logic ONLY in Domain\
✔ Use Cases in Application\
✔ Infrastructure implements interfaces\
✔ Controllers must be thin\
✔ Views display only

❌ No Eloquent in Domain\
❌ No DB queries in Domain\
❌ No business logic in Controllers\
❌ No logic in Views\
❌ No logic in Routes

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 6️⃣ DDD Requirements

Must include:

-   Entities\
-   Value Objects\
-   Aggregates\
-   Repository Interfaces (Domain)\
-   Repository Implementations (Infrastructure)\
-   Use Cases (Application)

Business rules MUST stay inside Domain.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 7️⃣ SOLID Enforcement

All code must follow:

-   Single Responsibility\
-   Open/Closed\
-   Liskov Substitution\
-   Interface Segregation\
-   Dependency Inversion

Constructor injection only.\
No static service access.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 8️⃣ Allowed Design Patterns

-   Repository Pattern\
-   Service Layer\
-   Factory Pattern\
-   DTO Pattern\
-   Dependency Injection\
-   Strategy Pattern (only when justified)

No unnecessary patterns.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 9️⃣ Database Rules (MySQL Only)

-   Proper indexing\
-   Foreign keys\
-   Constraints\
-   Normalization\
-   ACID compliance

Transactions REQUIRED for critical operations.\
No direct DB access outside Infrastructure.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 🔟 Laravel 12 Rules

-   Middleware registered in bootstrap/app.php
-   No Http/Kernel.php
-   No Console/Kernel.php
-   Use php artisan make: commands
-   Use Form Requests for validation
-   Use eager loading to prevent N+1
-   Use config() instead of env() outside config files

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Testing Policy

-   Pest v4 only
-   Feature tests preferred
-   Use factories
-   Use php artisan make:test --pest
-   Do not create verification scripts if tests exist
-   Activate pest-testing skill for test-related tasks
-   Always use version-specific search-docs

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Code Quality & PHP Standards

-   Run vendor/bin/pint --dirty
-   Always use explicit return types
-   Use constructor property promotion
-   Use PHPDoc blocks (no inline comments unless complex)
-   Use curly braces for all control structures
-   Enums use TitleCase keys

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1️⃣3️⃣ Frontend & UI Rules

## Responsive Design (MANDATORY)

The UI must:

-   Be fully responsive for Mobile, Tablet, and Desktop
-   Use flexible layouts (Flexbox/Grid)
-   Use relative units (rem, %, etc.)
-   Avoid fixed widths
-   Prevent layout breaking on small screens

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 🎨 Official Color Palette (MANDATORY)

Primary: #717980\
Secondary: #a0b0bf\
Light Accent: #d6d2cd\
Dark Accent: #4a545e

Rules:

-   Maintain visual consistency
-   Use primary for main actions
-   Use dark accent for headers
-   Use light accent for backgrounds
-   Do not introduce random colors

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1️⃣4️⃣ Offline Rule

-   No external APIs unless explicitly approved
-   No cloud dependencies
-   System must run locally
-   No runtime internet requirement

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1️⃣5️⃣ AI Behavioral Rules (CRITICAL)

The AI must:

-   Read this file before editing
-   Respect folder structure
-   Never mix layers
-   Never bypass Domain rules
-   Never inject business logic into Controllers
-   Never use Eloquent in Domain
-   Never change architectural direction
-   Always use Laravel Boost tools when required

If a request violates architecture → Refuse and suggest compliant
solution.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1️⃣6️⃣ Development Workflow (MANDATORY)

Every feature must follow this order:

1.  Define Domain Entity
2.  Add Business Rules
3.  Define Repository Interface
4.  Create Use Case
5.  Implement Infrastructure
6.  Connect via Controller

Never start from Controller.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 📌 FINAL RULE

This file is the single architectural authority. All generated code must
